 35S  c  2021Go09: {+26}Mg({+18}O,2|an){+35}S fusion-evaporation reaction. Exp 1
 35S 2c  determined the beam energy for producing high-spin states of {+35}S: an
 35S 3c  80-MeV {+18}O beam was delivered from the JAEA tandem accelerator      
 35S 4c  facility and impinged on a 0.5-mg/cm{+2} thick, self-supporting        
 35S 5c  metallic enriched foil of {+26}Mg. |g rays were detected using the     
 35S 6c  GEMINI-II array of 14 Ge detectors with BGO Compton - suppressor       
 35S 7c  shields. The reaction channel was selected by detecting the evaporated 
 35S 8c  charged particles with a 4|p silicon detector. Measured E|g, I|g,      
 35S 9c  |a|g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(ADO). Exp 2 used the same {+18}O beam energy, the
 35S Ac  same target, and the same charged-particle detectors as Exp 1. The beam
 35S Bc  was delivered from the ALTO-Tandem accelerator facility at IPN Orsay.  
 35S Cc  |g rays were detected using the ORGAM array of 13 Ge detectors based on
 35S Dc  the EUROGAM with the BGO scintillator for the anti-Compton suppressor. 
 35S Ec  Compared with large-scale shell-model calculations with the SDPF-MSD4  
 35S Fc  interaction. Also see 2015GoZY, 2014GoZZ, 2013GoZW, and 2012IdZZ.      
